Notebook[{Cell["Fitting MagneticTB bands to VASP", "Title"], Cell["To fit a tight-binding model to VASP bands, first \
read EIGENVAL and construct the Hamiltonian from symmetry. Here we fit three bands with a three-orbital model, compare \
nearest-neighbor and second-neighbor results, and then fit a selected energy or k-point range. Plot the fitted and VASP \
bands together to see both the agreement and any remaining differences.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData["Needs[\"MagneticTB`\"]"], "Input"], Cell["Read and inspect the three VASP bands", "Section"], 
  Cell["Use vaspEig to read bands 21-23 and subtract the Fermi energy. First plot all three bands to see the reference \
band structure:", "Text"], Cell[BoxData["eigenvalFile = FileNameJoin[{\n  NotebookDirectory[],\n  \"..\", \
\"ReferencePages\", \"Symbols\", \"EIGENVAL\"\n}];\nvaspBands = vaspEig[eigenvalFile, -0.0072, 1, 21, \
23];\nListLinePlot[\n  Transpose[vaspBands[[All, 2]]],\n  Frame -> True,\n  FrameLabel -> {\"k-point index\", \"Energy \
relative to efermi\"},\n  PlotRange -> All\n]"], "Input"], 
